---1. INTRODUCTION AND ACCEPTANCE
1.1. This Proprietary Software License Agreement ("Agreement" or "EULA") governs the installation, access, and use of the ConfigFars game and all related software, services, servers, websites, launchers, updates, content, and materials (collectively, the "Software").

1.2. The Software is licensed, not sold. It is proprietary, closed-source software owned and/or controlled by ConfigFars and is not Open Source.

1.3. You accept this Agreement by: (a) clicking "Accept"; (b) installing or using the Software; or (c) creating an account. Electronic acceptance has legal effect.

1.4. Eligibility. You represent that you have legal capacity to enter into this Agreement. If you are under the age of legal majority, you may use the Software only with parental consent.

1.5. If accepting on behalf of an organization, you represent that you are authorized to bind that organization.

---2. DEFINITIONS
"ConfigFars" means the ConfigFars brand, its development organization, owners, and the applicable rights holder.

"Software" means the game and all proprietary components supplied by ConfigFars, including executable files, source code, object code, game logic, systems, architecture, algorithms, netcode, APIs, graphics, textures, animations, models, maps, environments, characters, effects, audio, music, text, dialogue, documentation, databases, configuration files, and all updates, patches, and versions thereof.

"Proprietary Content" means all content, code, and materials owned or controlled by ConfigFars.

"Confidential Information" means non-public information including unreleased builds, beta content, roadmaps, source code, server architecture, and security mechanisms.

"Technical Protection Measures" means any licensing, DRM, encryption, authentication, anti-cheat, anti-tamper, or access-control mechanism.

"Cheat" means any software, hardware, script, or method that grants an unfair advantage or interferes with the Software.

"Third-Party Components" means software, libraries, services, or assets owned or licensed by third parties.

"Applicable Law" means all laws and regulations that apply to you or the Software.

