---8. PROHIBITED ACTIVITIES
Without written authorization from ConfigFars, you shall not:
8.1 Copying and Distribution
copy except as required for installation;
create or distribute cracked, pirated, or unauthorized copies;
upload to unauthorized websites, torrents, or file-sharing services;
sell, rent, lease, sublicense, or commercially distribute;
offer through unauthorized cloud gaming or streaming systems;
distribute license keys, codes, or accounts outside authorized channels.
8.2 Source Code and Technical Extraction
publish, disclose, leak, or distribute source code or Confidential Information;
obtain source code through unauthorized means;
extract, dump, or decrypt proprietary code or data;
reproduce internal systems or algorithms for redistribution.
8.3 Asset Extraction
Extract, rip, dump, or distribute any Proprietary Content: models, textures, maps, animations, sounds, music, images, characters, effects, shaders, scripts, game data, or databases.
8.4 Modification and Derivative Works
create modified versions of proprietary components;
create derivative works based on the Software;
create unofficial ports or clones;
redistribute modified copies;
integrate components into other products.
8.5 Commercial Exploitation
Use the Software for any unauthorized commercial purpose: products, services, games, applications, advertisements, websites, merchandise, paid tournaments, or "boosting" services.
8.6 Artificial Intelligence and Data Mining
use the Software or Proprietary Content to train, fine-tune, or develop AI or machine-learning models;
scrape, crawl, or data-mine from the Software, servers, or services;
use AI tools to generate content that replicates Proprietary Content.
8.7 Branding and Trademarks
Use ConfigFars names, logos, or trademarks in a manner that implies ownership, sponsorship, or endorsement, or register confusingly similar domains or social handles.
8.8 Security and Technical Protection
bypass or disable Technical Protection Measures;
circumvent authentication or licensing systems;
interfere with anti-cheat or integrity mechanisms;
gain unauthorized access to servers or infrastructure;
conduct DDoS attacks or scanning;
introduce viruses or malware.
8.9 Cheating and Abuse
Create, develop, sell, or use:
Cheats, hacks, aimbots, wallhacks, speed hacks;
bots, macros, or unauthorized automation;
injectors, trainers, or memory editors;
unauthorized clients or server emulators;
packet manipulation tools;
exploits or glitches for unfair advantage;
hardware devices for unfair advantage.
8.10 Conduct Toward Others
Harass, threaten, or abuse other users or ConfigFars staff; engage in fraud, phishing, or social engineering; engage in unauthorized real-money trading; or disrupt the Software.

